NNAAMMEE
     stty - set/print terminal modes

SSYYNNOOPPSSIISS
     ssttttyy [-tt_t_t_y_n_a_m_e] [_m_o_d_e ...]

DDEESSCCRRIIPPTTIIOONN
     With no _m_o_d_e arguments, ssttttyy prints the erase and kill
     characters, the special characters, the line speed, and the
     enabled modes of the standard output.  With _m_o_d_e arguments,
     ssttttyy sets each requested mode, character, or speed, and ap-
     plies them all at once after the whole command line has been
     parsed.

     Each _m_o_d_e argument is one of the following.  Any mode may be
     preceded by - to select its opposite, except where noted.

     _n_u_m_b_e_r       Set both the input and output line speed to
                  _n_u_m_b_e_r, a recognized baud rate: 00,  5500,  7755,
                  660000,  11220000,  11880000,  77220000,  99660000,  1199220000,  A
                  speed of 00 hangs up the phone (drops modem con-
                  trol) immediately.

     eevveenn         Use even parity.

     oodddd          Use odd parity.

     rraaww, -rraaww (also ccooookkeedd)
                  Enable, or disable, raw mode for both input and
                  output: disable all input and output character
                  processing (including erase/kill editing, sig-
                  nal characters, and newline mapping).

     rraawwiinn        Raw mode for input only.

     rraawwoouutt       Raw mode for output only.

     ccbbrreeaakk       Break out of a read after every input character
                  (character-at-a-time input) instead of waiting
                  for a full line.

     nnll           Disable mapping of carriage return to newline
                  on input.  -nnll restores the mapping (the
                  default).

     eecchhoo         Echo input characters as they are typed.

     llccaassee        Map upper-case input to lower case, for ter-
                  minals that cannot generate lower case.

     ttaabbss         Disable expansion of tabs to spaces on output.
                  -ttaabbss expands them (the default).

     ttaannddeemm       Enable tandem mode: start and stop output in
                  response to the ssttaarrtt and ssttoopp characters.


