     ccrrtt          Enable erase and kill processing suited to a
                  CRT terminal (which can back up and overwrite)
                  rather than a hardcopy terminal.

     eekk           Reset the erase and kill characters to # and @,
                  respectively.

     eerraassee _c      Set the character that erases the last-typed
                  character to _c.

     kkiillll _c       Set the character that erases the current input
                  line to _c.

     ssttaarrtt _c      Set the character that resumes output to _c.

     ssttoopp _c       Set the character that suspends output to _c.

     eeooff _c        Set the character that signals end of input to
                  _c.

     bbrreeaakk _c      Set the alternate line-break character to _c.

     qquuiitt _c       Set the character that raises a quit signal to
                  _c.

     iinntt _c        Set the character that raises an interrupt sig-
                  nal to _c.

     hhuupp          Hang up the line when the last process that has
                  the terminal open closes it.

     eexxccll         Reserve the terminal for exclusive use by this
                  process; a later ooppeenn by another process fails
                  until it is closed.  -eexxccll clears the reserva-
                  tion.

     fflluusshh        When the modes given on this command line are
                  applied, flush any pending input first. This is
                  the default.  -fflluusshh applies the modes without
                  flushing pending input.

     pprriinntt        Print the terminal's attributes (as with no ar-
                  guments), after applying any other modes given
                  on the same command line.

     Each character _c above may be given as a single literal
     character; as the word DDEELL; as \_o_o_o, an octal escape
     (leading backslash, up to three octal digits); as ^_x or
     ccttrrll-_x, a control character; or as the word ooffff, which dis-
     ables that character (no character will trigger the action).

     An option -tt_t_t_y_n_a_m_e names the terminal /ddeevv/_t_t_y_n_a_m_e to
     operate on, instead of the standard output; if given, it
