DDIIAAGGNNOOSSTTIICCSS
     ssttttyy complains if the standard output (or the terminal named
     by -tt) is not a terminal, if a _m_o_d_e word is not recognized,
     or if a character specification is badly formed.

NNOOTTEESS
     Whether a given mode has any effect depends on the terminal
     driver in use; requesting an unsupported mode is not itself
     an error.
